1013..1091 Comment "/// Rotating by `b` and back is the identity (cubical\'s `rotInv-1`, `b · a ·"
1092..1172 Comment "/// invLooper b ≡ a`, `_·_` associating to the left). The obligation over `a`"
1173..1247 Comment "/// holds `b` at its point, where `mul(Base, a)` is `a` and the loop moves"
1248..1320 Comment "/// through `mul`\'s second argument as itself; the one over `b` moves it"
1321..1396 Comment "/// through both of the outer `mul`\'s arguments, the loop then its inverse."
1397..1473 Comment "/// The square of the two loops is not owed: the paths of the circle are its"
1474..1491 Comment "/// words, a set."
